{"id":"a12103c3017bdc252cbb9acb9f40afe8cc2e8aa6","axis":"silent","repo":"k0sproject/k0s","sha":"a12103c3017bdc252cbb9acb9f40afe8cc2e8aa6","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"cmd/worker/worker.go","lines":["@@ -251,7 +251,7 @@ func (c *Command) Start(ctx context.Context, nodeName apitypes.NodeName, kubelet"," \t\t}"," "," \t\tsp := worker.NewStaticPods()","-\t\treconciler, err := nllb.NewReconciler(c.K0sVars, sp, c.WorkerProfile, *workerConfig.DeepCopy())","+\t\treconciler, err := nllb.NewReconciler(c.K0sVars, sp, c.WorkerProfile, *workerConfig.DeepCopy(), nodeName)"," \t\tif err != nil {"," \t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"failed to create node-local load balancer reconciler: %w\", err)"," \t\t}"],"additions":1,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"docs/configuration.md","lines":["@@ -355,6 +355,7 @@ Windows."," | `imagePullPolicy`            | The pull policy being used used for the Envoy Pod. Defaults to `spec.images.default_pull_policy` if omitted.                             |"," | `apiServerBindPort`          | Port number on which to bind the Envoy load balancer for the Kubernetes API server to on a worker's loopback interface. Default: `7443`. |"," | `konnectivityServerBindPort` | Port number on which to bind the Envoy load balancer for the konnectivity server to on a worker's loopback interface. Default: `7132`.   |","+| `patches`                    | Customizations applied to the Envoy Pod generated by k0s. See [Node-local load balancer patches](#node-local-load-balancer-patches).     |"," "," ##### `spec.network.nodeLocalLoadBalancing.traefik`"," ","@@ -367,6 +368,7 @@ for node-local load balancing."," | `imagePullPolicy`            | The pull policy being used used for the Traefik Pod. Defaults to `spec.images.default_pull_policy` if omitted.                             |"," | `apiServerBindPort`          | Port number on which to bind the Traefik load balancer for the Kubernetes API server to on a worker's loopback interface. Default: `7443`. |"," | `konnectivityServerBindPort` | Port number on which to bind the Traefik load balancer for the konnectivity server to on a worker's loopback interface. Default: `7132`.   |","+| `patches`                    | Customizations applied to the Traefik Pod generated by k0s. See [Node-local load balancer patches](#node-local-load-balancer-patches).     |"," "," ##### `spec.network.controlPlaneLoadBalancing`"," ","@@ -646,13 +648,15 @@ generate before those resources are written and applied. This is an escape"," hatch for adjustments k0s does not expose as dedicated config options. Patches"," live under the component they belong to:"," ","-| Component      | Config key                        |","-| -------------- | --------------------------------- |","-| CoreDNS        | `spec.network.coreDNS.patches`    |","-| kube-proxy     | `spec.network.kubeProxy.patches`  |","-| kube-router    | `spec.network.kuberouter.patches` |","-| Calico         | `spec.network.calico.patches`     |","-| metrics-server | `spec.metricsServer.patches`      |","+| Component      | Config key                                               |","+| -------------- | -------------------------------------------------------- |","+| CoreDNS        | `spec.network.coreDNS.patches`                           |","+| kube-proxy     | `spec.network.kubeProxy.patches`                         |","+| kube-router    | `spec.network.kuberouter.patches`                        |","+| Calico         | `spec.network.calico.patches`                            |","+| metrics-server | `spec.metricsServer.patches`                             |","+| NLLB (Envoy)   | `spec.network.nodeLocalLoadBalancing.envoyProxy.patches` |","+| NLLB (Traefik) | `spec.network.nodeLocalLoadBalancing.traefik.patches`    |"," "," Each entry selects a target resource by `kind` and `name` (optionally narrowed"," by `namespace`) and provides the patch `type` and `content`. The `content` may","@@ -695,6 +699,23 @@ spec:","                             memory: 256Mi"," ```"," ","+#### Node-local load balancer patches","+","+The patches for [node-local load balancing] (NLLB) differ from the other","+components' patches in a few ways:","+","+- They're applied by each worker node to the static Pod it runs, rather than by","+  the controllers. Changes only take effect after the k0s worker process has","+  been restarted.","+- The target is always `kind: Pod`, `name: nllb` and `namespace: kube-system`.","+  The `nllb-<node name>` Pods listed by `kubectl get pods` are mirror Pods,","+  whose names get the node name appended by the kubelet.","+- If the patches can't be applied, or result in an invalid Pod, the load","+  balancer runs without any of them, and a warning event is recorded on the","+  Node. See","+  [Customizing the load balancer Pod](nllb.md#customizing-the-load-balancer-pod)","+  for details.","+"," ## Disabling controller components"," "," k0s allows to completely disable some of the system components. This allows"],"additions":28,"deletions":7,"truncated":false},{"path":"docs/nllb.md","lines":["@@ -78,6 +78,65 @@ the new configuration to take effect."," "," [specapi]: configuration.md#specapi"," ","+## Customizing the load balancer Pod","+","+The Pod that runs the load balancer on each worker node can be customized","+using [patches], for settings that k0s doesn't expose as dedicated config","+options. Patches go into `spec.network.nodeLocalLoadBalancing.envoyProxy.patches`","+or `spec.network.nodeLocalLoadBalancing.traefik.patches`, depending on the load","+balancer type in use. Their target is always the Pod named `nllb` in the","+`kube-system` namespace. This is the name of the Pod as generated by k0s. The","+`nllb-<node name>` Pods listed by `kubectl get pods` are mirror Pods, whose","+names get the node name appended by the kubelet.","+","+For example, to give Envoy more time to drain in-flight connections when the","+node shuts down:","+","+```yaml","+spec:","+  network:","+    nodeLocalLoadBalancing:","+      enabled: true","+      type: EnvoyProxy","+      envoyProxy:","+        patches:","+          - target:","+              kind: Pod","+              name: nllb","+              namespace: kube-system","+            patch:","+              type: StrategicMergePatch","+              content: |","+                spec:","+                  terminationGracePeriodSeconds: 60","+```","+","+The patches are applied by the k0s worker process when it starts. Worker nodes","+that are already running must be restarted for changed patches to take effect.","+","+### When patches can't be applied","+","+If the patches can't be applied, or result in an invalid Pod (e.g. a changed","+name or namespace, or unknown fields), the load balancer runs without any of","+them. This keeps the node operational, since several of its components rely","+on the load balancer to reach the control plane. The error is logged by the k0s","+worker process, and a warning event is recorded on the Node:","+","+```console","+$ kubectl describe node worker-0","+...","+Events:","+  Type     Reason                             Age  From  Message","+  ----     ------                             ---  ----  -------","+  Warning  NodeLocalLoadBalancingPatchFailed  10s  nllb  Failed to apply patches to the node-local load balancer, running it without patches. Fix the patches in the cluster configuration and restart the worker. Error: ...","+```","+","+Note that the API server deletes events after a while, by default after one","+hour. To apply the patches, fix them in the cluster configuration and restart","+the k0s worker process on the affected nodes.","+","+[patches]: configuration.md#component-patches","+"," ## Full example using `k0sctl`"," "," The following example shows a full `k0sctl` configuration file featuring three"],"additions":59,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"inttest/nllb/nllb_test.go","lines":["@@ -53,6 +53,29 @@ func (s *suite) TestNodeLocalLoadBalancing() {"," \t\t\t\t\tif s.nllbType != \"\